      "content": "thanks for adding that. i noticed even in the first part you mentioned that \"protectionist backpedaling\" poses risks. it sounds like you're saying the critics are basically just reacting to an inevitable shift toward global cooperation. do you think there's any legitimate way to balance these concerns, or is the move toward this multilateral agreement just the only viable path forward for global stability?",
